Result: Demonic Forces Shattered               Result: Varnaz Dies; Lightborn Legend Born
🌋 Background Story: The Butcher of the Deep Rift
Varnaz was a creature born from the mutagenic, corrupting depths of the Ashen Rift—a violently erupting volcanic canyon deep within the Abyss. Standing at a colossal 220 cm, his anatomy is a nightmarish fusion of dense, demonic muscle and rigid, calcified bone plate carapaces that burst violently through his leathery, ash-purple skin. He didn't just command the legions; he was their living battering ram.

According to the lore novels, Varnaz earned his title by conquering the lawless tribes of the molten trenches through sheer, unadulterated violence. His face, completely warped away from humanity, featured a flat, reptilian nasal ridge, jagged obsidian bone-splinter cheekbones, and an exposed, skeletal outer jaw mechanism that housed rows of black iron teeth. Instead of hair, a wild, mohawk-like ridge of writhing, dark-crimson fibrous tendrils ran down his skull, constantly shedding hot ash and smoking embers like a dying volcano. He was a creature that personified the unstoppable momentum of the underworld—until his blades struck the Holy Light. His death at the hands of Tigreal's vanguard didn't just end his reign of terror; it altered the entire political landscape of the Abyss, forcing the remaining demon lords to realize that the human empire was no longer defenseless.

🪓 The Weapon: The "Rift-Reaver" Cleaver
Varnaz does not fight with tactical grace or finesse; he swings a weapon built for industrial execution. His chosen instrument of slaughter is the Rift-Reaver, a catastrophic, brutally oversized demonic cleaver measuring an astonishing 180 cm in length.

The Obsidian Edge
The Magma Core: The blade is forged from a rare, corrupted ore harvested from the deepest trenches of the Ashen Rift. The metal features a porous, dark purple surface that mimics the texture of cooled volcanic magma, accented by a glowing, jagged red edge that never loses its sharpness.

The Shield-Saw Spine: The spine of the blade is lined with thick, heavy iron teeth explicitly designed to saw through heavy knightly tower shields and crush defensive formations. The hilt is wrapped in the thick, coarse leather of a slain subterranean behemoth, finishing in a massive, spiked iron pommel that can crack stone with a single impact.

🖤 The Power: "Smoldering Ruin"
Varnaz’s presence on the battlefield is a suffocating, supernatural manifestation known as Smoldering Ruin. His magic does not require incantations; it flows naturally from his corrupted physiology and his symbiotic armor.

1. The Cloud of Suffocating Paranoia
Varnaz is constantly enveloped in a dense, rolling cloud of pitch-black smoke and deep crimson energy that distorts the air with extreme heat. This aura acts as a localized environmental hazard; as he marches, his massive digitigrade, three-toed iron-clawed boots permanently scorch, crack, and burn the very earth beneath him, leaving a trail of ruined ground that damages and slows any mortal entity trying to pursue him.

2. The Carnage Eye Activation
The center of his chest armor—the Carnage Cuirass, which is fused directly into his ribs and collarbone—features an embedded, weeping eye of dark abyssal magic. When Varnaz raises the Rift-Reaver to strike, this eye snaps open, blinking slowly while casting a hellish fire across the area. This projection inflicts a heavy, terrifying psychological dread that instantly drains the courage of nearby soldiers, reducing their physical attack damage and fracturing their morale.

3. Feral Talon Retaliation
Because his massive arms terminate in heavy, barbed iron gauntlets equipped with curved steel talons extending past his fingertips, Varnaz cannot be truly disarmed. If an enemy manages to knock the Rift-Reaver from his grip, his Smoldering Ruin aura flares into an explosive burst of hellfire, granting him a massive surge of attack speed and life-steal as he resorts to rending enemy armor to pieces with his bare, mutated claws.

🍖 The Twist: The Great Gourmet of the Underworld
Despite being an ageless, terrifying monument of unholy devastation who smells of sulfur, burning blood, and ash, the lore novels hint at a hilariously specific quirk regarding the late Abyssal General. Varnaz was an absolute connoisseur of human military rations—specifically, Moniyan dried beef jerky.

Intercepted campaign journals from his captains revealed that during his raids on imperial outposts, while his demonic legions were hunting for gold and glory, Varnaz would personally ransack the commissary tents. He reportedly found human food vastly superior to the glowing mushrooms and magmatic grubs of the Abyss. In fact, a popular rumor among the Winter Vanguard suggests that the real reason he launched his final, ill-fated invasion across the border wasn't actually for geopolitical dominance—he was just entirely out of snacks, and his favorite Moniyan smokehouse was located just past the front lines. Unfortunately for Varnaz, the Lightborn Squad served him a receipt he couldn't pay.
















Name: Arion, Chieftain of the Light-Blessed
The Radiantly Corrupted Physiology and Tragic Facial Structure
This character presents a profound and haunting transformation, standing as a physical monument to the absolute, consuming power of the Lord of Light. Once a mortal tribal leader, his human biology has been thoroughly overwritten by divine energy, resulting in a magnificent yet deeply unsettling stature that reaches a height of 195 cm. His body type is that of a high-density, heavily conditioned warrior-monarch, featuring broad shoulders and a powerful, muscular frame that appears entirely devoid of standard human body fat—instead, his muscle groups look as though they have been tightly bound with silver threads of pure energy. His facial structure is strikingly handsome yet terrifyingly rigid, looking like a flawless marble statue that has been brought to life. He appears to be a man in his late 30s, possessing a razor-sharp, chiseled jawline that lacks any human imperfection, and a tall, straight, aristocratic nose that gives him an air of supreme authority. His skin tone is an unnatural, hyper-bleached pearlescent white that subtly radiates a cold, internal golden light, so intense that it completely erases natural shadows beneath his eyes and jaw. His eyes are wide, piercing almond-shaped orbs that completely lack pupils or irises; they are instead solid pools of burning, liquid gold that leak faint trails of shimmering white smoke from their corners, conveying an expression of absolute, unblinking fanaticism and a complete loss of mortal empathy.

The Haloed Laurel and Crown of the First Theocrat
His head is adorned with an intricate, deeply symbolic headpiece that marks his transition from a tribal chieftain to the world’s first divine representative. He does not wear a standard war helmet; instead, he wears a heavy, open-faced crown forged from a unique, matte-white mineral that resembles polished ivory, which forms a jagged, defensive crest over his brow. Interlocking with this ivory crown is a golden laurel of metallic feathers, sculpted to mimic the wings of angels, which curves tightly around his temples and secures his magnificent hair. His hairstyle is a grand, flowing mane of thick, shimmering platinum-white hair that does not entirely respond to natural physics. While it cascades down past his shoulder blades in heavy, pristine waves, the top layers float in a slow-motion, weightless dance around his head, creating a constant, crown-like solar corona effect. Running down the center of his forehead, emerging from beneath the crown, is a vertical, glowing golden scar that bleeds pure light rather than blood—the permanent mark where the Lord of Light directly touched his mind.

The Aether-Plate Cuirass and High-Priest Vestments
The upper body attire of this character is a spectacular, seamless marriage of heavy, protective war-plates and ornate, liturgical vestments. He wears a heavy chest piece known as the Aether-Plate Cuirass, crafted from an experimental fusion of white marble and liquid gold that has no visible rivets or seams, looking as though it was molded around his torso by a divine hand. The center of the breastplate features an embossed sunburst sigil that pulses with a rhythmic, warm amber light, echoing his heartbeat. Around his neck is a heavy, ceremonial gorget of interlocking golden rings that supports a pristine, white silk hood, which is currently draped back across his shoulders to reveal his glowing mane. His massive shoulders are protected by grand, flaring pauldrons that sweep upward like angel wings, from which a long, heavy cape of crimson silk hangs down, its hem intricately embroidered with golden runes detailing the first laws of order. His forearms are encased in sleek, articulated silver vambraces that protect his wrists, ending in elegant white leather gauntlets adorned with solid gold trim along each individual fingertip.

The Sovereignty Faulds and Lower Body Armored Dreadnought
Securing his grand upper vestments at the waist is a wide, heavy battle-belt made of thick, white dragon-hide, fastened with a large, rectangular gold buckle that is deeply engraved with the layout of the first holy city. Hanging from this belt is a grand, multi-layered war-skirt composed of heavy, pristine white fabric panels that are reinforced with segmented golden plates, following the anatomical curve of his hips and thighs. Beneath this protective skirt, his lower body type is long, powerful, and built with the sturdy grace of a conquering general, clad in form-fitting Light-Weave hosiery of a pale, shimmering silver hue. His shins are encased in majestic, knee-high white-gold greaves with intricate filigree that depicts the historical timeline of the Light-Blessed tribe's ascension. These heavy leg plates taper down into elegant, pointed metal sabatons that do not fully press into the earth; instead, Arion floats a mere two inches above the ground, leaving a trail of scorched grass and tiny, fading golden flower-petals behind him as he moves forward.

The Scepter of Absolute Order and the Blinding Purity Aura
This character wields a catastrophic, beautifully terrifying weapon known as the "Scepter of Absolute Order"—a massive, two-handed polearm measuring an astonishing 210 cm in length. The shaft of the weapon is forged from a rare solar-iron that transitions beautifully from a deep bronze at the base to a blindingly bright silver at the top, wrapped in fine silver chains that rattle with a ghostly, metallic ring when swung. The head of the scepter features a complex, slowly rotating golden ring orrery that effortlessly suspends a miniature, burning sun at its absolute center, radiating intense heat and blinding light. The aura carried by this weapon, and Arion himself, is a suffocating, multi-layered field of pure, blinding white-gold energy that distorts the air around him. This aura smells strongly of fresh ozone and heavy temple frankincense, exerting an immense, paralyzing psychological weight on anyone nearby. When he channels his power, a massive, multi-winged shadowy silhouette of an ancient god manifests directly behind him, reflecting the overwhelming, tyrannical dominance of the primordial deity that possesses his soul.

Lore: The Tragically Blessed Architect of God's Will
Long before the foundation of the Moniyan Empire, Arion was a proud, fiercely protective human chieftain who led his nomadic tribe across the unforgiving, chaotic plains of the Land of Dawn. Desperate to protect his people from the terrifying beasts and the creeping corruption of the Abyss, Arion offered a desperate prayer to the sky, unknowingly opening his mind to the primordial deity of order—the Lord of Light. The god answered, but the divine blessing was a beautiful poison; it purged Arion's human flaws but completely erased his free will, converting him into a radiantly corrupted puppet. Driven by a fanatical, absolute devotion to order, Arion gathered his transformed "Light-Blessed" tribe and forced them to construct the world's very first theocratic city—a towering metropolis of white marble where human individuality was outlawed in favor of absolute obedience to the light. Arion became the first high priest and supreme ruler of this holy city, entirely forgetting his original humanity, living only to expand the Lord of Light's territory through relentless, holy crusades that offered the world a brutal choice: absolute submission to the light, or immediate purification by the sword.

Suggested Atmospheric Background
Arion would look exceptionally magnificent standing at the apex of a grand, towering white marble balcony overlooking his newly constructed theocratic city during a dramatic sunrise. The background should feature the endless, sweeping architecture of the holy city, with towering spires, golden domes, and massive white stone arches cutting through a sea of soft, low-lying morning clouds. The lighting should be a brilliant, cinematic "Divine Dawn," where the powerful, golden rays of the rising sun strike the city and filter sharply behind Arion, creating a majestic rim-light that catches the floating, platinum-white strands of his hair and reflects intensely off the polished surfaces of his white-gold armor. This high-contrast, heavenly lighting should highlight the pristine, unblemished textures of his marble-like skin and the glowing liquid gold of his eyes. A soft, shimmering mist of golden particles from his purity aura should be shown pooling around his floating sabatons, blending beautifully into the reflective marble floor of the balcony, capturing his terrifying, awe-inspiring presence as the absolute ruler of the first holy empire.

Before the Lightborn Squad ever wielded their legendary blades, and eras before the Moniyan Empire laid its first foundation stones, the Land of Dawn bore witness to a chilling dawn of absolute fanaticism.In the overarching historical texts and lore expansion novels, Arion, Chieftain of the Light-Blessed, stands as a magnificent, terrifying reminder that in this universe, "holy" does not automatically mean "good." He is famously recognized as the world's very first Theocrat—the tragic blueprint of what happens when a mortal man's noble intentions are completely devoured by a primordial cosmic entity.To the historical scholars of the Land of Dawn, Arion is legendary for building the first-ever holy metropolis out of pure white marble and gold. But more than his architecture, he is famous for his terrifying, unblinking eyes of solid liquid gold. He represents the terrifying, tyrannical face of absolute order—a man who traded his own soul, free will, and empathy to become a radiantly corrupted puppet for the Lord of Light.📜 Background Story: The Price of a Desperate PrayerLong before the world was mapped, Arion was a fiercely protective, deeply human tribal chieftain leading his nomadic people across the violent, monster-infested plains of the early Land of Dawn. Trapped between the creeping, horrific corruptions of the Abyss and the ravenous primordial beasts of the wild, Arion watched his people bleed season after season. Desperate, exhausted, and pushed to the brink of extinction, he climbed the highest peak, fell to his knees, and screamed a desperate prayer to the empty heavens for a salvation that could anchor his tribe.The heavens answered—but the salvation was a beautiful poison.The Lord of Light reached down, burning a vertical, glowing golden scar directly into the center of Arion's forehead. The divine energy instantly purged his human frailties, but it also completely bleached away his humanity, his memories, and his free will. His human heart was replaced by a cold, calculating machine of absolute divine order.Under this fanatical possession, Arion forced his transformed "Light-Blessed" followers to abandon their nomadic lives and build a towering, unyielding metropolis of white stone. Within its walls, human individuality, artistic deviation, and personal flaws were strictly outlawed. Arion became the supreme High Priest, leading bloody, unyielding crusades across the frontier. His campaigns offered the surrounding tribes a chillingly simple, binary ultimatum: bow down in absolute, unquestioning submission to the light, or be instantly purified by the edge of a sword.🔱 The Weapon: The "Scepter of Absolute Order"Arion marches into battle wielding a catastrophic, beautifully terrifying instrument of divine enforcement known as the Scepter of Absolute Order—a massive, two-handed polearm stretching an imposing 210 cm in length.The Engine of PurityThe Solar-Iron Shaft: The core handle of the polearm is forged from a rare, heavy solar-iron that naturally transitions from a rich, deep bronze at its base to a blindingly brilliant, polished silver at its apex. Fine, intricately linked silver chains wrap loosely around the column, rattling with an eerie, rhythmic metallic ring whenever the weapon is swung through the air.The Star-Orrery Head: The crown of the scepter features a complex, slowly rotating golden ring orrery. Suspended effortlessly at the absolute epicenter of these spinning metallic tracks is a miniature, roaring burning sun. This contained celestial anomaly constantly radiates intense, suffocating heat waves and a blinding glare that melts enemy steel armor on contact.☀️ The Power: Blinding Purity AuraArion’s presence on the battlefield does not merely inspire fear; it exerts a crushing, supernatural environment that physically and psychologically paralyzes anyone who stands against the cosmic designs of the Lord of Light.1. The Divine Corona & Weightless StrideArion does not plant his pointed metal sabatons into the dirt of the mortal world; he floats perpetually exactly two inches above the ground. As he moves, his radiant, platinum-white mane floats weightlessly in a slow-motion solar corona around his head crown. His movement leaves a scorched trail of burnt grass and tiny, rapidly fading golden flower petals, demonstrating his total rejection of earthly gravity.2. The Atmospheric Ozone SuffocationArion is enveloped in a dense, shimmering field of translucent white-gold energy fields that visibly warp and distort the surrounding air. This purity aura smells intensely of fresh, sharp ozone and suffocating temple frankincense. The raw, barometric spiritual weight of this aura acts as an invisible vice, causing enemy heroes to experience immense psychological dread, drastically slowing down their movement speed and locking away their ability to cast skills.3. The Multi-Winged Shadow ManifestationWhen Arion fully channels his cosmic power through the sun burst sigil on his Aether-Plate Cuirass, the golden trails of smoke leaking from his unblinking eyes expand violently. A massive, multi-winged shadowy silhouette of an ancient god manifests directly behind his 195 cm frame. This phantom avatar mirrors his movements, turning his basic physical strikes into sweeping, wide-area shockwaves of white-gold fire that completely vaporize Abyssal entities and mortal shields alike.🕊️ The Twist: The Bureaucratic Nightmare of ParadiseWhile the old history scrolls paint Arion as a grand, unmoving marble statue of holy terror, the deeper lore novels expose a hilariously petty, hyper-fixated side to the first Theocrat. Because his mind was overwritten to process absolute order, Arion became completely obsessed with microscopic, meaningless symmetry.According to ancient journals left behind by his disgruntled architects, Arion once halted an entire military crusade into prime enemy territory for three whole weeks because he noticed that one of the columns on a newly built public library was exactly two millimeters shorter than its twin on the left. He personally stood on his floating boots, glaring at the stone with his burning, pupil-less golden eyes, refusing to let his army march until the stonemasons chipped away at the marble to achieve perfect mathematical alignment.Furthermore, despite having zero human empathy left, he refuses to let anyone touch his pristine crimson silk cape. If a drop of mud or Abyssal blood splashes onto the golden runes embroidered on his hem, his aura flares so violently that the ambient temperature cooks nearby rations. He may be a grand, god-possessed conquering general, but he is also a cosmic neat freak who will pause a holy war just to make sure the world's lines are perfectly straight.



















Name: Morwen, The First Outcast of the Shadow-Followers
The Abyssally Tempted Physiology and Predatory Facial Structure
This character stands as a chilling, corrupted testament to the terrifying allure of absolute freedom offered by the Lord of the Abyss. Once a mortal man of leadership, his human biology has been aggressively reshaped by chaotic energies, granting him an imposing, unsettlingly tall stature of 200 cm. His body type is defined by a lean, elongated anatomy that possesses a terrifying, fluid grace, reminiscent of a nocturnal predator. His physical build is entirely composed of compressed living shadows and taut, wire-like musculature that seems to shift and ripple under his skin like liquid mercury. His facial structure is an arresting mix of gauntally sharp angles and dark, hypnotic beauty, making him appear as an individual in his early 40s who has been thoroughly consumed by forbidden knowledge. He features a razor-sharp, sunken jawline accentuated by high, deeply hollowed cheekbones that naturally pull his face into a perpetually mocking, predatory expression. His skin tone is a deep, matte obsidian-charcoal that actively absorbs surrounding light rather than reflecting it, creating a hollow, void-like appearance across his features. His eyes are deeply set, wide sockets containing two swirling whirlpools of chaotic violet energy; they completely lack pupils or irises, and thin trails of thick, black smoke constantly leak from their corners, burning with an unholy intelligence and an eternal, untamable defiance.

The Spiked Crown of Anarchy and the Fluid Midnight Mane
His head is defined by a chaotic, untamed arrangement of dark elements that visually scream his status as the father of all outcasts. He does not wear a traditional battlefield helmet or hood; instead, resting directly upon his brow is a jagged, asymmetrical crown forged from unyielding Dread-Iron. This crown looks less like a crafted object and more like a row of curved, horn-like obsidian shards growing violently out of his forehead, forcing his posture into an attitude of eternal, unyielding arrogance. His hairstyle is a voluminous, chaotic mane of midnight-black strands that flows wildly down past his shoulder blades. This living hair behaves as if it is constantly submerged in deep, turbulent water, moving with a heavy, independent life of its own, while the frayed tips occasionally flicker out into wisps of cold, dark-purple flame. Piercing through the shadows of his hair are elongated, slightly pointed ears adorned with small silver rings that rattle softly, further distancing his appearance from that of a standard human being and pushing him into the realm of a demonic demigod.

The Dread-Iron Carapace and Tattered Abyssal Silk
The upper body attire of this character is a dark masterpiece of fractured, asymmetrical design, reflecting the chaotic philosophy of the Abyss. He wears a jagged breastplate of dark, iridescent Dread-Iron that appears to have fused directly into his chest, looking like a living carapace that grew naturally from his flesh. At the absolute center of this metal torso is an embedded, oval gem known as the Eye of the Void, which pulses with a deep, sickening magenta light. Around his neck sits a high, spiked iron gorget that forces his chin upward, emphasizing his distain for authority. Over his broad, uneven shoulders rests a heavy, tattered mantle crafted from Abyssal Silk—a smoke-captured, semi-material fabric split into multiple serrated, ribbon-like ends that flutter and drift behind him even in the absence of wind. His long, powerful arms are encased in articulated, clawed gauntlets of fractured iron, with each finger tapering into an impossibly sharp obsidian point capable of tearing through physical space and leaving micro-fissures of purple energy in the air.

The Dragon-Scale Tassets and Scorched Under-Armor
Securing his dark vestments at the midsection is a low-slung, heavy combat belt made from tattered, blood-crimson leather, fastened by a large, interlocking dragon-skulls buckle. Hanging from the belt to guard his hips and thighs is a heavy, overlapping tasset composed of dark, jagged dragon-scale plates, each one deeply etched with forbidden Shadow Abyss runes that glow with a faint, malevolent magenta luminescence. Beneath these protective plates, his lower body type is long, agile, and built for explosive, serpentine speed. He wears form-fitting, dark bruised-purple tactical trousers that are cross-stitched with heavy silver threading. His shins and lower legs are protected by massive, knee-high iron greaves that end in sharp, wing-like metal protrusions at the sides, designed to deflect oncoming strikes. These heavy leg guards lead down into heavy, pointed metal sabatons that press firmly into the earth; however, with every step this character takes, his boots visibly sink into the terrain, leaving cracked, scorched footprints that bubble with volatile, hissing purple energy.

The Scepter of Eternal Night and the Suffocating Miasma
This character wields an ominous, catastrophic polearm known as the "Scepter of Eternal Night"—a massive, seven-foot-long weapon of total ruin. The shaft is crafted from the twisted, petrified bone of a primordial abyssal beast, wrapped tightly in cold silver chains that rattle with a ghostly, hollow sound whenever the weapon is brandished. The head of the scepter features a massive, jaggedly curved dark crystal blade that houses a violently swirling vortex of dark energy at its center, crackling with erratic arcs of violet lightning. The aura carried by this weapon, and Morwen himself, is a thick, suffocating Presence of Dread that manifests as a heavy, hazy purple-and-black miasma. This field distorts the lighting around him and carries the bitter, ancient scent of sulfur and cold, rusted metal. When his power peaks, this thick fog expands upward, projecting a massive, multi-eyed shadowy silhouette of a monstrous god directly behind his back, visually anchoring him as a being who answers only to the dark, chaotic whims of the void.

Lore: The Sovereign of the Lawless Wilds
Long before the modern factions of the Land of Dawn drew their borders, Morwen was an influential human chieftain who ruled a massive, nomadic clan. When the neighboring tribes submitted to the tyrannical, mind-altering order of Arion and the Lord of Light, Morwen refused to bow, viewing their absolute order as nothing more than a beautiful, golden slavery. Desperate to find the power necessary to defend his people's free will, Morwen ventured into the forbidden depths of the earth, where he was tempted and ultimately altered by the Lord of the Abyss. The dark god granted him unparalleled cosmic power but exacted a terrible price, twisting his body into an obsidian nightmare and instilling in him an insatiable hunger for chaos. Returning to the surface, Morwen shattered the traditional laws of his people and led them away to establish the world's very first anarchic community—a lawless, sprawling sanctuary built within jagged volcanic chasms where the only true rule was absolute personal freedom. As the First Outcast, Morwen became a dark ideological icon, leading savage, midnight raids against the white marble cities of the Light-Blessed, fully believing that true freedom can only be achieved when every empire, tower, and law is burned to absolute ash.

Suggested Atmospheric Background
This character would look exceptionally magnificent standing at the precipice of a jagged, volcanic cliff overlooking a vast, subterranean city of fire and iron. The background should feature the chaotic architecture of his anarchic settlement, with rough-hewn stone fortresses, hanging rope bridges, and massive iron chains stretching across a deep cavern illuminated by rivers of glowing, violet-purple magma. The lighting should be a dramatic, high-contrast "Abyssal Eclipse," where the dark, hot glow of the underground lava fields casts deep, demonic red and purple under-lighting onto his matte-obsidian skin and the sharp contours of his Dread-Iron armor. Wisps of thick, black smoke and glowing magenta ash should be shown drifting lazily upward from the bubbling terrain below, curling around his heavy, pointed sabatons and weaving through the tattered strands of his midnight-black mantle. This dark, cinematic lighting perfectly captures his position as a defiant, predatory king ruling over a realm of eternal night and absolute, unchained chaos.



🏛️ The Mythic Lore: The Primordial Split of the Land of Dawn
Every coin has two faces, and the ancient history of the Land of Dawn is no exception. While the first high priest, Arion, was busy erecting his flawless, tyrannical white marble towers of absolute order, a counter-force was brewing in the dark trenches of the earth.

In the forbidden, unwritten chapters of Moniyan history, Morwen, The First Outcast of the Shadow-Followers, is celebrated—and feared—as the absolute architect of rebellion. He is famous for being the world's very first anarchist. He didn't just reject the beautiful, golden slavery offered by the Lord of Light; he marched straight into the dark abyss to fetch the weapon needed to shatter it. To the scholars of the occult, Morwen is legendary for establishing the first lawless sanctuary within the molten chasms of the world, proving that freedom is a flame that burns brightest in the pitch black.

